---
/**
 * /legal/privacy — required before Phase 10's forms collect anything (§8.3).
 *
 * The single most important property of a privacy policy is that it is TRUE, so
 * this describes what the site actually does today rather than boilerplate:
 * localStorage is not a cookie, saves never leave the device, analytics is off,
 * and the Google Fonts request genuinely does disclose an IP address to Google.
 * That last one is a real trade-off and is named rather than glossed over.
 *
 * Not legal advice, and it says so. It needs a review before any data is
 * collected.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, analyticsEnabled } from "../../lib/site";

const updated = "27 August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  pathname="/legal/privacy/"
  description="What Isoperia does and does not collect. No accounts, no cookies, saves stay on your device."
>
  <section class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          {site.name} has no accounts, sets no cookies, and does not transmit your game saves
          anywhere. The site is static. What follows is the detail, including the one third-party
          request the site does make.
        </p>

        <h2 id="saves">Your game saves</h2>
        <p>
          Saves are stored in your browser — <code>localStorage</code> with an IndexedDB backup
          — and are never uploaded. Nobody, including us, can read them. That is why there is
          no account to create.
        </p>
        <p>
          The flip side is real and worth stating plainly: because the save lives only in
          your browser, clearing your site data, using a different browser, or a private
          window with no stored data will lose it. The game can export a save to a file,
          and you should do that for anything you would miss.
        </p>

        <h2 id="storage">Browser storage, not cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The site stores one preference — your light or dark theme choice — under the key <code
            >isoperia-theme</code
          >. This uses
          <code>localStorage</code>, which is not a cookie: it is never attached to a
          network request and never leaves your device. That is also why there is no
          cookie banner; there are no cookies to consent to.
        </p>

        <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
        {
          analyticsEnabled() ? (
            <p>
              A cookieless analytics service records page views in aggregate. It sets no
              cookies, assigns no identifier, and does not track you between sites or
              sessions.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              There is currently <strong>no analytics on this site at all</strong> — no
              page-view counter, no session recording, nothing. If that changes it will be
              a cookieless service that sets no cookies and assigns no cross-site
              identifier, and this page will be updated before it goes live.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2 id="fonts">There is no third party</h2>
        <p>
          This site contacts no external host. Everything it loads — including its
          typefaces — is served from this domain, and its content security policy permits
          nothing else, so there is no request from this site that could disclose your IP
          address or user-agent to anyone but us.
        </p>
        <p>
          That was not always true. The typefaces were loaded from Google Fonts until 28
          August 2026, which disclosed your IP address and user-agent to Google on every
          page view, and this page said so. They are self-hosted now and both Google hosts
          have been removed from the policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by Netlify, which keeps standard server access logs (IP
          address, requested URL, timestamp, user-agent) as part of operating any web
          server. We do not add to those logs or use them for anything beyond diagnosing
          faults.
        </p>

        <h2 id="not-here">What the site does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No advertising, and no ad networks.</li>
          <li>No third-party trackers, pixels, or fingerprinting.</li>
          <li>No embedded social widgets, comment systems, or chat.</li>
          <li>No selling or sharing of data, because there is none to sell.</li>
          <li>No email address is collected anywhere on the site today.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
        <p>
          The site collects nothing from anyone, so there is nothing collected from
          children either.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If the site starts collecting anything — a newsletter signup, for instance —
          this page will say so before that goes live, and the date at the top will
          change.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>
            This page is written to be accurate rather than to be legally comprehensive,
            and it has not been reviewed by a lawyer. It should be reviewed before the
            site collects any personal data.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding-block: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
